 "note": "WHAT THIS ARCHIVE PHYSICALLY HOLDS, as opposed to what it has read. Every file in sources/archive-scans, which is a CUSTODY store and is deliberately not published: library- and archive-supplied material is kept so that a quotation can be checked, not so that it can be redistributed. No built page references this directory and a gate keeps it that way. WHY IT EXISTS: on 23 September 2026 four pages of this site were quoting two documents at length - the 1830 Kolbe letter and the 1992 DSAB typescript - which existed only in a Downloads folder. The archive had read them, transcribed them, tested them line by line and cited them, and held neither. Nothing could have told anybody, because custody was not written down anywhere a tool could read it. It is written down here now, and checkregisters refuses a build where this file and the directory disagree in either direction. WHAT IT CANNOT DO, said plainly: it cannot tell whether a sentence on a page claiming to have READ something is true. That is a discipline and not a gate, and pretending otherwise would be the more dangerous error.",
